  (text "VIA $C000.  PA0-PA7 keyboard rows (pulled up, low = pressed).  PB0-PB2 and CA2\nform a 4-bit column select (CA2 = bit 3) into the 74HC154 on the keyboard\nPCB, which drives the selected column low.  Columns 0-7: 64-key matrix.\nColumn 15: joystick, whose DE-9 port is on the keyboard PCB; with it selected,\nROW0-ROW4 read up, down, left, right, fire.  Columns 8-14 unused.\nSD card (SPI, bit-banged): PB3 MOSI, PB4 SCK, PB5 CS, PB6 MISO (BIT sets V),\nCA1 card detect.  Module: microSD breakout with 3.3 V regulator and level\nshifter (e.g. Adafruit 254: 5V, 3V, GND, CLK, DO, DI, CS, CD).  Check the\nmodule pin order and that its MISO high level meets the VIA input threshold.\nPB7 = timer 1 square wave to the speaker.  CB1 = VDP frame interrupt.\nCB2 spare on a header (can be a second sound voice from the shift register).\nKeyboard connector: 1 +5V, 2/7/8 GND, 3-6 KB_SEL0-3, 9-16 ROW0-7." (at 25.4 196.22 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 269d41e1-12be-48ac-85db-aab56d480f4c)
  )
)
